# Line endings. Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true); files that run or are
# read inside Linux containers keep the LF endings they were tested with (bash rejects CRLF: "$'\r': command not found").
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
